Sashimi, really, which is plain raw fish (or raw
cuttlefish, IIRC), as opposed to sushi, which is a
lot of stuff used to flavor / enhance a staple food
base, much like peanut butter and jelly does for
bread.

Some of that flavoring is raw fish, but it can also
be fish roe, sea urchin eggs, raw mammal flesh,
smoked fish,...). Characteristicly it is wrapped
decoratively using seaweed as a wrapping medium,
with pressed rice (or rarely scrambled eggs) as a
base staple foodstuff onto or within which to wrap
the flavoring bits.

Often with some vegetable matter or other additions
are used as well (celery, avocado, cooked egg white,
...) the lot wrapped into e.g. the classic
"California roll".

But then, that's some of that quibbling again.


